Table full name: bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.part_d_prescriber_2014
Column name: npi Type: STRING Description: National Provider Identifier
Column name: nppes_provider_last_org_name Type: STRING Description: Last Name/Organization Name of the Provider
Column name: nppes_provider_first_name Type: STRING Description: First Name of the Provider
Column name: nppes_provider_city Type: STRING Description: City of the Provider
Column name: nppes_provider_state Type: STRING Description: State Code of the Provider
Column name: specialty_description Type: STRING Description: Provider Specialty Type
Column name: description_flag Type: STRING Description: Source of Provider Specialty
Column name: drug_name Type: STRING Description: Name of the drug
Column name: generic_name Type: STRING Description: Generic name of the drug
Column name: bene_count Type: INT64 Description: Number of Medicare Beneficiaries
Column name: total_claim_count Type: INT64 Description: Number of Medicare Part D Claims, Including Refills
Column name: total_day_supply Type: INT64 Description: Number of Day's Supply for All Claims
Column name: total_drug_cost Type: FLOAT64 Description: Aggregate Cost Paid for All Claims
Column name: bene_count_ge65 Type: INT64 Description: Number of Medicare Beneficiaries Age 65+
Column name: bene_count_ge65_suppress_flag Type: STRING Description: Reason for Suppression of Bene_Count_ge65
Column name: total_claim_count_ge65 Type: INT64 Description: Number of Claims, Including Refills, for Beneficiaries Age 65+
Column name: ge65_suppress_flag Type: STRING Description: Reason for Suppression of Total_Claim_Count_Ge65, Total_Drug_Cost_Ge65, and Total_Day_Supply_Ge65
Column name: total_day_supply_ge65 Type: INT64 Description: Number of Day's Supply for All Claims for Beneficiaries Age 65+
Column name: total_drug_cost_ge65 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Aggregate Cost Paid for All Claims for Beneficiaries Age 65+
Column name: total_30_day_fill_count Type: FLOAT64 Description: The aggregate number of Medicare Part D standardized 30-day fills. The standardized 30-day fill is derived from the number of days supplied on each Part D claim divided by 30. Standardized 30-day fill values less than 1.0 were bottom-coded with a value of 1.0 and standardized 30- day fill values greater than 12.0 were top-coded with a value of 12.0.
Column name: total_30_day_fill_count_ge65 Type: FLOAT64 Description: The number of Medicare Part D standardized 30-day fills for beneficiaries age 65 and older. The standardized 30-day fill is derived from the number of days supplied on each Part D claim divided by 30. Standardized 30-day fill values less than 1.0 were bottom-coded with a value of 1.0 and standardized 30-day fill values greater than 12.0 were top-coded with a value of 12.0.
